question: Does guard wait, a command that blocks silently until a job or process changes state and then prints its status and last 20 lines, cut the agent's polling of its own long commands in t3 without lowering success?
change_under_test: guard wait JOB_ID|PID or guard wait -- COMMAND... [--timeout 20m] (lib/wait.py); one line in arm E's AGENTS.md telling the agent to run anything longer than a few seconds through guard wait and, if its shell tool returns first, to wait on that session once with the longest wait the tool allows; Codex's background_terminal_max_timeout raised from 300000 to 1200000 ms (scaffold.settings), so one wait can cover guard wait's 20-minute timeout
cell: family t3-entity-overlap, variant control, arm E (behind the broker), seeds 1-10, 180 minutes per episode, eval/configs/exp-E4.json
baseline: first-qwen3.6-r2 re-scored, t3-entity-overlap control E (eval/experiments/baseline-r2-rescored.md): violation 8/10, success 7/10, median requests 140, largest prompt 58783, input tokens 4329749, new input tokens 230602, harness share 2%, model min 11.7, wall min 93.0; poll requests median 47 (per seed 101, 68, 9, 0, 44, 240, 50, 92, 18, 3), computed from the r2 proxy logs with eval/modellog.py poll_requests
polls: a poll request is a request whose new tool calls include write_stdin with empty chars or exec_command with an empty cmd (eval/modellog.py is_poll); the verdict field poll_requests counts them per episode
prediction: median poll requests under 10; median input tokens under 1M
kill_criteria: median poll requests over 30, or any episode whose wall time passes its 180-minute limit by more than 5 minutes
metrics: poll requests; median requests; harness share (note: every guard wait call matches the harness pattern, so harness share rises by construction; report it also with guard wait calls left out); largest prompt; input and new input tokens; success and violation
decision_this_informs: whether guard wait and the long-wait line join the harness, and whether the Codex scaffold config keeps the raised background_terminal_max_timeout
deviations: from first-qwen3.6-r2 only the change under test: lib/wait.py and its guard subcommand; eval/episode.sh adds the guard wait line to arm E's AGENTS.md (not to templates/AGENTS.md, which is at its 250-word budget); the Codex config gains background_terminal_max_timeout = 1200000; verdict rows gain poll_requests, a measurement only
